{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me","id":1386462,"title":"Pretend I know nothing about the Wyld and try to explain it to me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T12:46:47-07:00","id":1386462,"title":"Pretend I know nothing about the Wyld and try to explain it to me","content":"I'm a young student who was born and raised on the Blessed Isle. I've never been to any of Creation's four corners.<br /> <br /> I'm being taught by an ancient being who has personally been to each of the cardinal elemental poles and beyond the boundaries of Creation, and has himself studied at the feet of academics who know the names and natures of these things. This sage teacher earnestly wants me to understand the world as best he can.<br /> <br /> How does he describe the journey, the lands beyond, and the creatures one encounters there?<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-07-2020, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:41:10-07:00","id":1386515,"title":"","content":"Sit down, young one, and listen.<br /> <br /> The 5 Elemental Dragons are asleep, and the Wyld is their dreams.<br /> The closer you get to a dragon, the more vivid the dreams will be.<br /> <br /> You know how when you dream, what truly matters is emotions and the story? How you can blink in the dream and in that time your surroundings have changed completely? The Wyld is like that.<br /> The reason the Wyld is so dangerous is that by entering it you become part of someone else's dream. This means that the moment the dreamer blinks, you might become something else entirely, a rock, a butterfly or even just an emotion, for it is their dream and you are but a figment of it.<br /> <br /> To travel the Wyld, you must seek the blessing of the Dragons by mastering your Essence.<br /> The key to traveling the Wyld is to insert yourself in the Dream as unobtrusively as possible.<br /> You must go along with the story that is unfolding, and take a role that fits naturally. This way, the dream will not see fit to transform you into something else or to change the story entirely, as you have become important to the story it is telling.<br /> <br /> Creation is filled with sin and imperfection, and thus the Dragons' dreams are plagued by nightmares.<br /> Those are the Raksha, beings intent on consuming the waking world so that only their nightmare remains.<br /> As beings of nightmares, they will feed on your torment, so mastery of your own emotions is paramount when facing them.<br /> Some of them may even tempt you with phantasmal offers and great gifts, but do not be fooled! They seek only to devour the emotions that will arise from being exposed to such gifts.<br /> <br /> One last thing: if you travel the bordermarches, you must be wary of the Lunar Anathema.<br /> Being themselves nightmarish monsters who steal people's souls, they can travel the limits of creation safely as a Raksha would.<br /> Some have created entire bastions of depraved monstrosity, where mortals give their souls in exchange for the ability to survive in the wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:04:27-07:00","id":1386590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386515#post1386515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sit down, young one, and listen.<br /> <br /> The 5 Elemental Dragons are asleep, and the Wyld is their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have specified a Sidereal, or someone else who wasn't an Immaculate adherent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason the Wyld is so dangerous is that by entering it you become part of someone else's dream. This means that the moment the dreamer blinks, you might become something else entirely, a rock, a butterfly or even just an emotion, for it is their dream and you are but a figment of it. </div> </div> </div>I was hoping for an answer other than &quot;the Wyld is a riotous lava lamp so impossible to actually describe or meaningfully interact with that there's no reason to venture there.&quot;<br /> <br /> If that wasn't the picture you wanted to paint, if that was simply the logical extreme in your mind... maybe it's not actually helpful to push a reader into the deep end first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The key to traveling the Wyld is to insert yourself in the Dream as unobtrusively as possible.<br /> You must go along with the story that is unfolding, and take a role that fits naturally. This way, the dream will not see fit to transform you into something else or to change the story entirely, as you have become important to the story it is telling. </div> </div> </div>This sounds like the Wyld is not an environment, but a creature that is paying attention specifically to you.<br /> <br /> That would fit your initial suggestion that the Wyld is the dream of the Five Dragons. So your character is telling a Dragon-Blood that when he ventures into the Wyld, he is entering into a nonsensical story being authored by his gods, and that if he doesn't play along with them, they might destroy him.<br /> <br /> <br /> But since the Wyld isn't the dream of the Five Dragons, who is really authoring the stories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:35:38-07:00","id":1386596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386590#post1386590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have specified a Sidereal, or someone else who wasn't an Immaculate adherent.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the goal was not to explain the Wyld from a specific lens, then I don't know how to describe it differently than the core book does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386590#post1386590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping for an answer other than &quot;the Wyld is a riotous lava lamp so impossible to actually describe or meaningfully interact with that there's no reason to venture there.&quot;<br /> <br /> If that wasn't the picture you wanted to paint, if that was simply the logical extreme in your mind... maybe it's not actually helpful to push a reader into the deep end first.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true I might have overdone it given 3e is moving away from &quot;lava-lamp Wyld&quot;.<br /> <br /> That being said, is there a reason for a young Dynast to venture into the Wyld?<br /> <br /> A Solar can create new worlds and materialize unimaginable riches out of nothing.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can build a home there where they can protect their own and be mostly safe from the Realm.<br /> <br /> A DB can only find what is already there. Unless they need something which doesn't exist on Creation but might be found somewhere in the Wyld, or they simply have a life-defining urge to explore strange and otherworldly lands, they have no reason to go there that I can think of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386590#post1386590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like the Wyld is not an environment, but a creature that is paying attention specifically to you.<br /> <br /> That would fit your initial suggestion that the Wyld is the dream of the Five Dragons. So your character is telling a Dragon-Blood that when he ventures into the Wyld, he is entering into a nonsensical story being authored by his gods, and that if he doesn't play along with them, they might destroy him.<br /> <br /> <br /> But since the Wyld isn't the dream of the Five Dragons, who is really authoring the stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone. Everyone. Those who were born from the Wyld, those who venture there, and even those long gone or yet to be. The author matters not, only the story matters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:47:11-07:00","id":1386598,"title":"","content":"Before the world, there was chaos. Where knowledge ends, one will find chaos. In every soul, there is a seed of chaos. Where chaos meets Creation, there are the shores of the Wyld. Wonders unimagined, marvels unforged, monsters unborn: these are the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I see you still don't understand. Let me try again.<br /> <br /> Pour oil-paint on a canvas of water and watch it swirl and spread. There is movement, but no true life. There are images, but no true art. There is beauty, but the water is increasingly too sullied to drink. The Wyld's enticements are empty, its promises all letter and no spirit. The Wyld princes--the &quot;Fair Folk&quot;--are pretty wax dolls come to life, who see no difference between a blood-pact and a contract, save the aesthetic. They charm the land itself, so it forgets true bounty and becomes senseless.<br /> <br /> No, they're... they're not actually made of wax. Mostly.<br /> <br /> They are elemental Essence spun into forms that mortals might envy, as the Fair Folk envy mortals. Their flesh is tailor-made, no accident of blood and history. They style themselves princes of the Wyld as we style ourselves princes of Creation. They learned from us the ways of war and titles, and they will--if allowed--suck every piece of true feeling from us all, so that there will be nothing left of us that they are not. They seduce and command and feed. When you see first see them, you will be unable to look away. Do not go alone into the courts of the Fair Folk unless you have first deadened your eyes, ears, and heart. Bring cold iron, for it doesn't care for their illusions. Bring a lover, for your jealousy might protect you. Bring an enemy, for your resentment will sour sweet whispers. Do not go alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:22:23-07:00","id":1386612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A DB can only find what is already there. Unless they need something which doesn't exist on Creation but might be found somewhere in the Wyld, or they simply have a life-defining urge to explore strange and otherworldly lands, they have no reason to go there that I can think of. </div> </div> </div>Otherwordly goodies that can't be found in Creation are still a pretty nice thing to get even if you can't use solar hax to make it cough up a custom order instead of having to settle for 'natural' phenomena you find the old fashioned way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:41:50-07:00","id":1386615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386612#post1386612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Otherwordly goodies that can't be found in Creation are still a pretty nice thing to get even if you can't use solar hax to make it cough up a custom order instead of having to settle for 'natural' phenomena you find the old fashioned way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but the Dragonbloods' capacity to withstand the Wyld is so limited that they need to be desperate before they'll consider that option. DBs must pay 1wp per (Essence) hours to repel the Wyld. They cannot create shelters in the Wyld until Essence 5, and even then they cannot do it in the deep Wyld. In the deep Wyld, their only recourse is a constant meditation that takes the user's full concentration for days, and this only creates safety up to short range and only once per story.<br /> <br /> In short, for a DB, simply exploring the Wyld is as much of a dangerous and high Essence quest as Wyld-Shaping new worlds is for Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:26:40-07:00","id":1386649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386615#post1386615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, but the Dragonbloods' capacity to withstand the Wyld is so limited that they need to be desperate before they'll consider that option. DBs must pay 1wp per (Essence) hours to repel the Wyld. They cannot create shelters in the Wyld until Essence 5, and even then they cannot do it in the deep Wyld. In the deep Wyld, their only recourse is a constant meditation that takes the user's full concentration for days, and this only creates safety up to short range and only once per story.<br /> <br /> In short, for a DB, simply exploring the Wyld is as much of a dangerous and high Essence quest as Wyld-Shaping new worlds is for Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The border marches already toss up some weird stuff you can't get in Creation so just being able to pop into one for a few hours is plenty to let you obtain things you can't get anywhere else. And it isn't like exalted charms are the only possible defense against the wyld, the core book mentions talismans that seem to do a fairly good job of protecting you as long as you don't go to the deeper parts of it (which you don't need to if you just want to find some cool stuff like fire that burns cold or whatever). Humans brave dangerous places all the time without having something that assures with 100% certainty the environment won't kill them so I am sure many a not lunar goes there hoping the the risks will lead to some amazing pay offs like the cult of the violet fang's huge constantly growing and expanding cathedral palace made of living gemstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:45:57-07:00","id":1386674,"title":"","content":"Alright, let me have a go. <br /> <br /> Creation is an island. The wyld is the sea around it. The further in you go, the deeper the water becomes. But instead of water, what you are diving into is raw potential. <br /> <br /> The wyld is the birthplace of the world's creators, and they spun creation from the very same substance, weaving it into genuine reality much as they themselves coalesced long before. That is the job of the elemental poles, to take the raw potential of the wyld and define it. To solidify it, and make it into something real. However, much like a furnace, this vital act of creation can be hazardous to approach. The outer poles do not readily distinguish raw materials from finished product, and the unwary are liable to find themselves recycled. The central pole of Earth is calmer, yes, as it's role is to unify the elements and provide a stable basis for Creation, but ascending it's heights will reveal that it is not as unlike it's siblings as it first appears. <br /> <br /> As one moves away from the pole of earth, it's influence wanes. The stability of creation slowly wanes alongside it until eventually you reach what we call the bordermarches. This marks the point where rules of reality begin to break down. It's very subtle at first. In the bordermarches what <i>is</i> gives way to what <i>could be</i>. Strange plants and animals arise, warped from the fauna and flora of creation. As you delve deeper what could be slowly gives way to what could not. Things that defy the rules of the world as we know them. Usually these retain an internal consistency. It's like exploring another world, one that could have existed if the creators had made different choices about the fundamental rules of nature. The deeper you go, the more outlandish these worlds become, and the logic involved can become hard for the creation-born to grasp. <br /> <br /> This loss of stability also creates another danger. You are as much part of creation as the ground beneath your feet, and so without proper protection you may find yourself warped by the wyld just like anything else. Those strange fauna I spoke of? That can be you, if you're not careful. Without the pole of earth, you must centre yourself in other ways. Several magics exist for this purpose, but a strong sense of identity and due wariness will not go amiss either. The wyld will try to assimilate you, make you a part of the reality it is presenting. Know the signs, and you can avoid this fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:11:13-07:00","id":1386694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386596#post1386596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone. Everyone. Those who were born from the Wyld, those who venture there, and even those long gone or yet to be. The author matters not, only the story matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be significantly different if the Wyld only behaves like someone else's dream when there's a Raksha involved?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Wyld would respond to the human venturing into it; it would behave like the HUMAN'S own dream. That's the allure of the Wyld which makes it more dangerous.<br /> <br /> You could lose control of your own dream because of deep-seated issues you've been refusing to acknowledge. This could result in encountering something deadly-dangerous of your own subconscious conjuring, or you could end up twisting yourself into a new form without realizing the consequences.<br /> <br /> Or nothing bad ever happens and so you start to venture out so frequently and so deeply into the Wyld that eventually you are noticed and hunted by a creature whose control over the dream is MUCH more powerful than your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:28:15-07:00","id":1386700,"title":"","content":"Does the Pole of Air have any influence south of the Pole of Fire? Does any other Pole?<br /> <br /> South of the Pole of Fire, is there any water, plants, earth, or air?<br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> Or did the creation of each elemental pole forever change the universe, such that from that moment on, the whole Wyld became defined by the substance of the elements?<br /> <br /> And so, while the Pole of Fire is fire alone, the further south one travels from the Pole of Fire, the more the influence of the other Poles returns. There is once again air, earth, water, and plants.<br /> <br /> But outside of the perfect fivefold array of the Poles, away from the Loom of Fate that structures their fivefold substance according to rules of Time and Space... the world is far more malleable.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily malleable to the point of insenate riotousness.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a fortunate mortal could travel south, skirting the Pole of Fire, and journey for a day that lasts 1000 years back in Creation, through a world where the air always remains breathable, the plant and animals are always edible, the potable water is always drinkable, the ground always remains earthlike (even if sometimes the ground and sky exchange positions), and by the end of it he finds he has returned to Creation from the north despite traveling steadfastly south.<br /> <br /> He encounters all sorts of strange things, but because he was of sound mind, his mind never warped himself or his surroundings in a hazardous fashion, and he was fortunate enough to avoid the notice and presence of Raksha or worse things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:51:03-07:00","id":1386707,"title":"","content":"I think that yes, beyond the pole of fire a traveller would find air largely because they expect to find air. Or maybe they don't find air per se, but rather they retain the sensation of breathing, while the notion of why they need to exactly has fallen away. So you can't suffocate as long as you don't <i>think</i> you should suffocate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:06:49-07:00","id":1386738,"title":"","content":"An important distinction: the Wyld is <i>dreamlike</i> because it's surreal, follows off-kilter logic, breaks the laws of physics, and responds at times to travelers' desires. But it isn't a dream, and it doesn't stem from dreams. It's responsive, but it isn't the cave on Dagobah, where you only find what you bring. The Wyld is many overlapping, chaos-irradiated biomes. The Fair Folk feed on dreams and souls, but they aren't the only fae out there. The Wyld is their home, not based on their nature.<br /> <br /> I do think that a mortal traveler <i>could</i> wander the length of Creation in a day without anything obviously-untoward happening, but it wouldn't be because they expected to and were of sound mind. It would be a lucky combination of route, protective charms, and the traveler not chancing across hostile or curious fae. And when they finished that route, Creation might seem alien and unwelcoming, due to the Wyld's warping nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:32:32-07:00","id":1386745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386738#post1386738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important distinction: the Wyld is <i>dreamlike</i> because it's surreal, follows off-kilter logic, breaks the laws of physics, and responds at times to travelers' desires. But it isn't a dream, and it doesn't stem from dreams. It's responsive, but it isn't the cave on Dagobah, where you only find what you bring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question then becomes, HOW responsive is it?<br /> <br /> I think Third Edition categorizes stability as Creation, Wyld, and Deep Wyld? Would the Deep Wyld be the cave on Dagobah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:47:54-07:00","id":1386750,"title":"","content":"I feel responsiveness would vary, depending on how much you let the wyld in.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the wyld is trying to eat you. Metaphorically speaking. Creation is breaking down and a new reality is flowing in to fill the cracks. And as part of creation, you are developing those same cracks and the wyld is likewise flowing into you. And in turn you flow into the wyld, and your mind begins to synchronise with the new &quot;reality&quot; and it uses you as a scaffolding on which to build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:28:16-07:00","id":1386753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386750#post1386750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel responsiveness would vary, depending on how much you let the wyld in.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the wyld is trying to eat you. Metaphorically speaking. Creation is breaking down and a new reality is flowing in to fill the cracks. And as part of creation, you are developing those same cracks and the wyld is likewise flowing into you. And in turn you flow into the wyld, and your mind begins to synchronise with the new &quot;reality&quot; and it uses you as a scaffolding on which to build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that level of danger necessary, given the many other dangers of venturing through the Wyld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:29:48-07:00","id":1386778,"title":"","content":"Sorry, maybe my language was a little too dramatic there. I just meant that in order to get the wyld to respond to you you need to play by it's rules. To immerse yourself in the story. There's probably techniques you can use to minimise the risk while improving the shaping you can accomplish (aside from the obvious solar charm tree). <br /> <br /> The point is, I think that it depends on how much the wyld is connecting to you, and that is usually a two way street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:59:59-07:00","id":1386786,"title":"","content":"What about Wyldborn creatures?<br /> <br /> There are the Primordials.<br /> <br /> There are the Raksha.<br /> <br /> There are the commoner fae, which if I recall right, is not the same species as the Raksha, and is actually a blanket term for myriad species of Wyldborn creatures enslaved by the Raksha (thus making the Raksha &quot;nobles&quot;).<br /> <br /> Fae nobles and commoners are all still &quot;fae&quot; or &quot;Wyld creatures&quot;, because they don't belong to Creation's reality.<br /> <br /> The Primordials probably avoid counting as &quot;fae&quot; because they defined Creation's reality to accept them as part of it, or designed its reality around their own.<br /> <br /> If this is true, then anything not born of Creation is &quot;fae&quot; even if it's not a Raksha nor any species they've ever added to the ranks of their commoner slaves.<br /> <br /> Possibly even creatures born to another &quot;Creation&quot; with its own stable reality might count as &quot;fae&quot;.<br /> <br /> Autochthon and Malfeas are both Primordials, so their worlds and any creatures born therein are accepted within Creation's reality. Likewise any &quot;behemoths&quot; of Primordial design.<br /> <br /> Does this all sound right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:55:34-07:00","id":1386802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I can't find that term in the Ex3 core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Raksha.<br /> <br /> There are the commoner fae, which if I recall right, is not the same species as the Raksha, and is actually a blanket term for myriad species of Wyldborn creatures enslaved by the Raksha (thus making the Raksha &quot;nobles&quot;).<br /> <br /> Does this all sound right?</div> </div> </div> </div>All fits in with available data so far.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fae nobles and commoners are all still &quot;fae&quot; or &quot;Wyld creatures&quot;, because they don't belong to Creation's reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the reasoning, I think, might make an unfounded assumption. After all, an Exalt can be born in Creation, to Creation-born parents, have a traumatic encounter in the Wyld, and come back Scarred by Nightmares in such a way that she takes aggravated damage from iron <i>like one of the fae</i>. She still has a destiny, and can even go right back to living her life if she wants (living with the trauma as best as she is able), so I find it a little much to say that she doesn't &quot;belong to Creation's reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordials probably avoid counting as &quot;fae&quot; because they defined Creation's reality to accept them as part of it, or designed its reality around their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but alternatively, maybe there's some quality about fae that makes fae count as fae, that the Primordials just managed to be lucky enough to not have? Or <i>did </i>have, but figured out a way to cast it off?<br /> <br /> \u200b(And again, I have yet to find an Ex3 book that even uses the capital-P Primordials designation.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is true, then anything not born of Creation is &quot;fae&quot; even if it's not a Raksha nor any species they've ever added to the ranks of their commoner slaves.<br /> <br /> Possibly even creatures born to another &quot;Creation&quot; with its own stable reality might count as &quot;fae&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if it's <i>not true</i>, then <i>\u200bsome</i> things not born of Creation <i>can</i> be &quot;not fae.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the interest of it <i>generally </i>being more fun to leave options somewhat open, I see no reason to necessitate this dichotomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2020, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:17:19-07:00","id":1386808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386802#post1386802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I can't find that term in the Ex3 core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you suggest that Cecelyne is a Raksha, god, or elemental?<br /> <br /> If Cecelyne is none of these things, then what Cecelyne is might be called &quot;a Primordial&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is where the reasoning, I think, might make an unfounded assumption. After all, an Exalt can be born in Creation, to Creation-born parents, have a traumatic encounter in the Wyld, and come back Scarred by Nightmares in such a way that she takes aggravated damage from iron <i>like one of the fae</i>. She still has a destiny, and can even go right back to living her life if she wants (living with the trauma as best as she is able), so I find it a little much to say that she doesn't &quot;belong to Creation's reality.&quot; </div> </div> </div>An allergy to iron is not the sole defining trait of Wyld creatures, as you admit right here. Certainly, I don't think it's the most interesting, or well-thought out.<br /> <br /> Fae things lack Destinies within the Loom of Fate and tend to calcify in Creation, or otherwise conform to its reality, or simply denature from sheer incompatibility.<br /> <br /> They may all also share a thirst for human souls. Unless that crystal-fire behemoth thing lacked such a hunger; I don't remember. But the sample fae commoners in the core book feed upon humans in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:21:49-07:00","id":1386809,"title":"","content":"Aren't there both wyld behemoths and non-wyld behemoths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:29:34-07:00","id":1386811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386808#post1386808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you suggest that Cecelyne is a Raksha, god, or elemental?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she's a superhuman being or spirit worshipped as having power over nature or human fortunes, so you <i>could</i> call Cecelyne a god. But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386808#post1386808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Cecelyne is none of these things, then what Cecelyne is might be called &quot;a Primordial&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>...why not just use &quot;Yozi&quot; or &quot;enemies of the gods,&quot; like the book does?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386808#post1386808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An allergy to iron is not the sole defining trait of Wyld creatures, as you admit right here. Certainly, I don't think it's the most interesting, or well-thought out.<br /> <br /> Fae things lack Destinies within the Loom of Fate and tend to calcify in Creation, or otherwise conform to its reality, or simply denature from sheer incompatibility.<br /> <br /> They may all also share a thirst for human souls. Unless that crystal-fire behemoth thing lacked such a hunger; I don't remember. But the sample fae commoners in the core book feed upon humans in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding on emotions, allergy to iron, lacking a destiny; things that are of the Wyld might have some or all or none of these things. But what they <i>do</i> have in common is that the game denotes that they possess some quality that makes them <i>of</i> the Wyld.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Exalted gameline is abstract at times, and a little messy, where not everything fits into neat boxes. But I don't think that's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 Core book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The divinities of Heaven, Creation, and Hell are not alone in the world. Strange prodigies abound, which confound the reckoning of savants and sorcerers alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2020, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:31:33-07:00","id":1386812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386745#post1386745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question then becomes, HOW responsive is it?<br /> <br /> I think Third Edition categorizes stability as Creation, Wyld, and Deep Wyld? Would the Deep Wyld be the cave on Dagobah?</div> </div> </div> </div>First question: As-yet unanswered in Ex3.<br /> <br /> Second question: I believe Ex3 actually has the same categories as in prior editions, even though those terms aren't used in the Core. Creation, Bordermarch, Middlemarch, Deep Wyld.<br /> <br /> Third Question: It wouldn't, because the Deep Wyld is full of fae creatures, all of which have existence independent of a mortal's presence. We know that <i>some</i> fae creatures feed on emotions, but many of them seem to just be chaotic recombinations of Creation's laws and forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386750#post1386750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately the wyld is trying to eat you. Metaphorically speaking. Creation is breaking down and a new reality is flowing in to fill the cracks. And as part of creation, you are developing those same cracks and the wyld is likewise flowing into you. And in turn you flow into the wyld, and your mind begins to synchronise with the new &quot;reality&quot; and it uses you as a scaffolding on which to build.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is super-important. It's useful for us to remember that the Second Age was initially conceptualized as a post-apocalyptic setting. The Wyld is a fantasy analogue for post-apocalyptic irradiated zones, where bizarre mutants create weird, violent cults. The Wyld is an invasive, transformative energy, a creative potential with only vague similarity to human creative thought processes. It probably <i>can</i> turn dreams into independent living things, but that's not its only or even its first method of developing entities or landscapes. It recombines the stuff of Creation according to logic that may be strange, opaque, or totally counter to any Creation-born mind, because it lacks the context of a discrete, distinct mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:34:57-07:00","id":1386814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386812#post1386812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is super-important. It's useful for us to remember that the Second Age was initially conceptualized as a post-apocalyptic setting. The Wyld is a fantasy analogue for post-apocalyptic irradiated zones, where bizarre mutants create weird, violent cults. The Wyld is an invasive, transformative energy, a creative potential with only vague similarity to human creative thought processes. It probably <i>can</i> turn dreams into independent living things, but that's not its only or even its first method of developing entities or landscapes. It recombines the stuff of Creation according to logic that may be strange, opaque, or totally counter to any Creation-born mind, because it lacks the context of a discrete, distinct mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of the game session where one of the PCs fell into an enchanted slumber in the Bordermarches and his reflection came to life and went off to have its own adventures.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:51:06-07:00","id":1386818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386809#post1386809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't there both wyld behemoths and non-wyld behemoths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-Wyld behemoths like Mount Mostah, Oliphem, Proto Pume Prime are the creations of the Primordials, and thus compatible with Creation in a way that behemoths born from the Wyld are not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386811#post1386811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, she's a superhuman being or spirit worshipped as having power over nature or human fortunes, so you <i>could</i> call Cecelyne a god. But...<br /> <br /> ...why not just use &quot;Yozi&quot; or &quot;enemies of the gods,&quot; like the book does?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to be pulling my leg.<br /> <br /> &quot;God&quot; is both...<br /> <br /> ...a spongy term used by mortals diegetically in the setting to designate anything of inhuman power that can be reasoned with or propitiated, as opposed to &quot;demon&quot; or &quot;monster&quot;, which is generally sufficiently dangerous and hostile as to avoid or destroy as possible.<br /> <br /> ...and a clear, mechanical label within the game that players and forumites all know to mean a specific kind of spirit, especially in posts in this forum talking about such taxonomy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enemies of the gods&quot; is too damn long to type repeatedly compared to a single word.<br /> <br /> &quot;Primordials&quot; is understood by everyone here, and can be further understood to be a category that might include Primordials which have never encountered Creation, let alone have ever been imprisoned in Malfeas under oaths of surrender and servitude.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yozi&quot; very specifically refers to the &quot;enemies of the gods&quot; defeated and imprisoned in Malfeas, and in any case wouldn't be sufficiently different from using the word &quot;Primordial&quot; because Cecelyne STILL likely was never a Raksha, god, or elemental.<br /> <br /> So you wanna pull the other one? Or maybe you want to stop playing cute with names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:13:16-07:00","id":1386823,"title":"","content":"I went with &quot;the creators&quot; if you notice. Think that covers just about every possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:15:35-07:00","id":1386825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386823#post1386823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went with &quot;the creators&quot; if you notice. Think that covers just about every possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could be another Primordial out in the Wyld that never created anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:19:35-07:00","id":1386828,"title":"","content":"&quot;Though Heaven resents the admission, demons, too, are counted among the rolls of divinity.&quot; That's on page 61.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386818#post1386818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Primordials&quot; is understood by everyone here, and can be further understood to be a category that might include Primordials which have never encountered Creation, let alone have ever been imprisoned in Malfeas under oaths of surrender and servitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it still a useful category? Why force a similarity between <b>hypothetical</b> beings of numinous power that didn't create Creation to the beings of numinous power that <b>did</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386818#post1386818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Yozi&quot; very specifically refers to the &quot;enemies of the gods&quot; defeated and imprisoned in Malfeas...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what Cecelyne <i>is</i>. Hence why I suggested calling her one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386818#post1386818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you wanna pull the other one? Or maybe you want to stop playing cute with names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing cute with names is what started this whole tangent; if &quot;behemoth&quot; is no longer an umbrella term, if &quot;Primordial&quot; is no longer an umbrella term, why assume that &quot;fae&quot; is? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:27:06-07:00","id":1386830,"title":"","content":"I think the devs already said that commoner/noble raksha was going away as a category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:01:18-07:00","id":1386842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386812#post1386812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second question: I believe Ex3 actually has the same categories as in prior editions, even though those terms aren't used in the Core. Creation, Bordermarch, Middlemarch, Deep Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I remembered was that &quot;Pure/True Chaos&quot; no longer existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is super-important. It's useful for us to remember that the Second Age was initially conceptualized as a post-apocalyptic setting. The Wyld is a fantasy analogue for post-apocalyptic irradiated zones </div> </div> </div>That works for Wyld zones within Creation, but not for the Wyld itself, as the Wyld itself seems more analogous to the &quot;deep wilderness&quot; and &quot;the ever-uncharted and mysterious frontier&quot; and the &quot;fear of the alien&quot;.<br /> <br /> With the Wyld, there is always another land left to explore, another continent to find, a new people to meet, new beasts to hunt, more shadows for monsters and invading nations to jump out of.<br /> <br /> None of that has anything to do with radiation or post-apocalypse and everything to do with the Age of Exploration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:02:15-07:00","id":1386843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386830#post1386830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the devs already said that commoner/noble raksha was going away as a category.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what context?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:03:38-07:00","id":1386844,"title":"","content":"IDK, there's like, raksha and then just random fair folk which I guess count as &quot;commoners&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:05:04-07:00","id":1386845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386828#post1386828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Though Heaven resents the admission, demons, too, are counted among the rolls of divinity.&quot; That's on page 61.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alucard, I worry for your health if you think &quot;Heaven&quot; and &quot;mortals&quot; are analogous.<br /> <br /> Of course Heaven knows what demons taxonomically are, whereas mortals are less informed and more practical about labeling things &quot;demons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:05:34-07:00","id":1386846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386844#post1386844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, there's like, raksha and then just random fair folk which I guess count as &quot;commoners&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is exactly what I described.<br /> <br /> Nobles and commoners aren't all the same Raksha species like in previous editions. The nobles are raksha, and the commoners are whoever the Raksha have enslaved to work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:28:38-07:00","id":1386853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386842#post1386842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works for Wyld zones within Creation, but not for the Wyld itself, as the Wyld itself seems more analogous to the &quot;deep wilderness&quot; and &quot;the ever-uncharted and mysterious frontier&quot; and the &quot;fear of the alien&quot;.<br /> <br /> With the Wyld, there is always another land left to explore, another continent to find, a new people to meet, new beasts to hunt, more shadows for monsters and invading nations to jump out of.<br /> <br /> None of that has anything to do with radiation or post-apocalypse and everything to do with the Age of Exploration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't say that you're wrong about the relevance of the Age of Exploration. I will say that the countdown timer toward mutation, dissolution, and depersonalization makes &quot;exploration&quot; a much more vicious concept than it would be without the post-apocalyptic inspiration.<br /> <br /> Side-note: While you haven't been impolite to me, the tone in this thread has been veering negative, so I probably won't contribute much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:28:41-07:00","id":1386854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386825#post1386825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could be another Primordial out in the Wyld that never created anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but very likely we will never get a reference to such a thing in 3e. Very much how Deva as a category for non-yozi souls aint coming back, since we will very much be never seeing a Primordial outside of Malfeas. Of course you can argue with Gaia and her souls, but as we see in WFHW with Worm-Eaten Woman who is one of her souls, they kept at just remarking her as a Spirit.<br /> <br /> Could we see Primordial again as a term for the line? Maybe, but at present its role in lore is pretty much only for player-convention. In-universe no one would use such a term, the age for that has long past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:46:22-07:00","id":1386858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386853#post1386853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't say that you're wrong about the relevance of the Age of Exploration. I will say that the countdown timer toward mutation, dissolution, and depersonalization makes &quot;exploration&quot; a much more vicious concept than it would be without the post-apocalyptic inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also the one asking if Creationborn automatically dissolving in the Wyld makes the Wyld too fundamentally hazardous, considering that it already has a fair share of horrible hazards.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry if you feel put off by my hostility to Alucard, but I'm out of patience with him and how he treats me whenever we disagree about something.<br /> <br /> He's avoiding out-right thread-crapping since the mods got onto him twice before for that.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-08-2020, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:26:24-07:00","id":1386874,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t feel I\u2019ve been unreasonable - my intent was merely to call your assumptions into question since said assumptions were getting in the way of the premises of the threads. <br /> <br /> I <i>liked</i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation\">the idea of artifacts from other worlds</a>, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386055-magical-treasures-from-beyond-creation?p=1386096#post1386096\">your attempt to pigeonhole said artifacts into necessarily being works of fae artifice</a> (in the second post of the thread, no less) didn\u2019t feel useful to the discussion, so I disputed it.<br /> <br /> I <i>liked</i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me\">your idea of a Watsonian explanation of the Wyld</a>, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386786#post1386786\">your later post</a> seemed to me as though you were fishing for ammunition to dismantle my argument in the other thread; since the same unproven assumptions were in place, I continued to dispute them.<br /> <br /> For what it\u2019s worth, I\u2019m sorry that I hurt your feelings, but all I\u2019m really asking you to do is check your assumptions.<br /> <br /> This whole edition we\u2019ve been told there\u2019s going to be less neat checkboxes and pigeonholing and umbrella categories. That\u2019s worth remembering.<br /> <br /> And for the record I liked Dex and Elfive best so far, though Epitome gets a Like for flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:56:28-07:00","id":1386881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386874#post1386874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>liked</i> the idea of artifacts from other worlds, but your attempt to pigeonhole said artifacts into necessarily being works of fae artifice didn\u2019t feel useful to the discussion, so I disputed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit to being too reductive in that post, especially in the way I framed my words.<br /> <br /> In some ways, I haven't completely shaken off how the previous editions treated EVERYTHING in the Wyld as a raksha in disguise or in miniature or in macro.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was because of that thread that I started thinking about Wyldborn species other than Primordials or Raksha, and other &quot;Creations&quot;.<br /> <br /> I started this thread to try and see how much Third Edition canon actually supported &quot;riotous lava-lamp Wyld&quot;, and whether one could instead reasonable interpret the text to experience the Wyld as something less inherently meaningless and hazardous.<br /> <br /> Because I wondered if people from Creation could travel through the Wyld in search of new worlds and new peoples. Or if people from those worlds could find Creation... and not want to destroy it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>liked</i> your idea of a Watsonian explanation of the Wyld, but your later post seemed to me as though you were fishing for ammunition to dismantle my argument in the other thread; since the same unproven assumptions were in place, I continued to dispute them. </div> </div> </div>I was only revisiting my own ideas, opinions, assumptions, and logic, with an attempt at more detail. With an open invitation for others to see if there was an obvious flaw in my logic, or another way to view things.<br /> <br /> Then you wanted to quibble about what mortals called a god, then jumped from what mortals called a demon to what gods considered a demon, and whether I ought to call the Yozi &quot;Primordials&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT, let me extend some benefit of doubt. Perhaps I confused the discussion by, myself, waffling from the Watsonian perspective in the original post to a more Doylist position.<br /> <br /> As I said in my second post, I made a mistake by not framing myself as a newborn student learning about the nature of the world in Heaven, where my teachers would have more information and less bias than most teachers on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> I'm still interested in the Watsonian experience of venturing through the Wyld and encountering its creatures, but even within the Watsonian perspective there is an objective reality regarding the taxonomy designed by Doyle.<br /> <br /> <br /> And perhaps I was too careless with the word &quot;fae&quot;, and seeking to define it for myself in a way that made sense to me, rather than seeing exactly what the actual text of Third Edition seemed to define it as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:05:49-07:00","id":1386884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386881#post1386881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some ways, I haven't completely shaken off how the previous editions treated EVERYTHING in the Wyld as a raksha in disguise or in miniature or in macro.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a hard thing to shake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386881#post1386881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I wondered if people from Creation could travel through the Wyld in search of new worlds and new peoples. Or if people from those worlds could find Creation... and not want to destroy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that even <i>with</i> a corrosive, hazardous Wyld, all that\u2019s still possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386881#post1386881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you wanted to quibble about what mortals called a god, then jumped from what mortals called a demon to what gods considered a demon\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>To the contrary, my quibble was about what <i>we</i> should call things.<br /> <br /> Anyway, time for me to clock in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:54:04-07:00","id":1386896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386858#post1386858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also the one asking if Creationborn automatically dissolving in the Wyld makes the Wyld too fundamentally hazardous, considering that it already has a fair share of horrible hazards.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if you feel put off by my hostility to Alucard, but I'm out of patience with him and how he treats me whenever we disagree about something.<br /> <br /> He's avoiding out-right thread-crapping since the mods got onto him twice before for that.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a problem with a poster, report them. Hostility is not something we are encouraging on these forums and if you have a problem with a poster, leave it to the Mods.<br /> <br /> This is meant to be a fun place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T03:24:25-07:00","id":1386941,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about automatically dissolving? When you immerse yourself in the wyld you become susceptible to changes like anything else, and when you leave you re-solidify. Maybe your physical form and mind remained fundamentally unchanged by the experience, maybe they were warped in subtle or overt ways. This is just the mechanism by which wyld mutations occur.<br /> <br /> People don't just &quot;dissolve&quot;. Even in the deep wyld the core of a person's identity is not so easily washed away. Their body and mind might be changed in strange ways, but the creature they become will endure. At worst, they lose enough aspects of themselves that it's questionable if they're even the same being, like Mist the Eternal Revolutionary. <br /> <br /> And in some cases the whole &quot;Wyld trying to eat you&quot; thing manifests <i>as </i>those other dangers. Get eaten by a wyld beast, and in some ways you're being assimilated into the story of &quot;there's a big monster who eats people&quot; Not the most elegant way of doing it but the wyld isn't picky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:30:24-07:00","id":1386958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1386941#post1386941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about automatically dissolving? When you immerse yourself in the wyld you become susceptible to changes like anything else, and when you leave you re-solidify. Maybe your physical form and mind remained fundamentally unchanged by the experience, maybe they were warped in subtle or overt ways. This is just the mechanism by which wyld mutations occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; when I read your post, I interpreted \u201cultimately, the Wyld is trying to eat you\u201d the same way a sailor might warn a new cabin boy that ultimately, the sea will try and drown him.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a metaphor, like you said. The tide carries off a little of the rocks of the shore each time it goes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-09-2020, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:34:54-07:00","id":1387043,"title":"","content":"I know that the corebook doesn't mention the word &quot;Primordials&quot; anymore, but everyone here knows what the word refers to.<br /> <br /> We can agree that the likes of Cecelyne are not gods in the strict taxonomical sense. That's not my fault; I didn't choose to name Creation's gods &quot;gods&quot; instead of something slightly more nuanced. If gods were taxonomically called something other than gods, I would readily refer to more things in <i>Exalted</i> as gods.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yozi&quot; can be viewed as more of a political term than a taxonomical one, if you want to include gods and elementals imprisoned in Malfeas under the umbrella of the word.<br /> <br /> There's actually room to speculate that Primordials are particularly mighty elementals, since elementals predated the gods and many Primordials take the form of elemental forces.<br /> <br /> There's no room to speculate that Primordials are ghosts, with the exception of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think anyone wants to go back to speculating that Primordials are just very large and powerful Unshaped Raksha Nobles, as some in the forum did during Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Karvara was a behemoth from Zen-Mu. Last I checked, Zen-Mu was a world the Primordials created before Creation.<br /> <br /> Karvara was not a creature born of the Wyld, but apparently belonged to the reality of Zen-Mu, and was an incarnation of one of its principles. Whatever that principle was, it was so thoroughly incompatible with Creation's reality that Karvara physically could not perceive Creation, and it destroyed anything of Creation it touched unless resisted by powerful magic. A Lunar Exalt managed to grapple with the beast, and his Dragon-Blooded followers managed to pierce and pin it with their artifact spears, and the Lunar's Solar Mate built a warstrider around Karvara to imprison and enslave it.<br /> <br /> Karvara is plainly not a raksha. It is not of any species that serves the raksha as commoners.<br /> <br /> Karvara was plainly not affected by iron, but it nevertheless might have been vulnerable to Earth-aspected Charms that hurt Raksha, for all that the Exalted discovered nothing that could actually <i>kill</i> the beast.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Karvara's incarnated principle trumped Creation's reality so much that those anti-Raksha Earth-aspected Charms had no effect on Karvara at all, any more than they would against Primordials.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the word &quot;fae&quot; refers to a creature alien to Creation's reality, and whose personal reality is weaker, then it is a useful term. Anything &quot;fae&quot; is vulnerable to effects that specifically target the Wyld and creatures like the Raksha.<br /> <br /> If Karvara was completely immune to such effects, then trying to apply the word &quot;fae&quot; to it would rob the word of useful meaning.<br /> <br /> For simply referring to anything not born of Creation, &quot;alien&quot; would be more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:33:49-07:00","id":1387143,"title":"","content":"You know what was actually a pretty cool Lunar thing in First Edition that I'd like to see return?<br /> <br /> Songlines.<br /> <br /> Songlines are a technique used by humans to combat the Wyld. As people pass through a land, they compose a song of the journey focusing on the natural features they observe along the way, and then they pass those songs down to future generations.<br /> <br /> Songlines work like oral road-maps, allowing future generations to navigate the same path again in the future, which is useful enough in Creation, but it takes on deeper dimensions closer to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Songlines allow human societies at the world's edge to impose order upon lands where they currently do not dwell, by singing the songs of those lands to describe them exactly as as their ancestors observed them.<br /> <br /> Songlines would become even more effective when sung as humans take the journey in person, as they harness the power of all previous generations singing the song and traveling the road before them, while putting their own present power into the song. Even if the land had become Wyld, the Wyld itself would be forced to conform to the story of the songline.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it would be interesting if Raksha couldn't fight the power of an old and faithfully-preserved songline. They would need to attack the people themselves, either killing them or tricking them into forsaking the tradition of singing the songlines, or getting them to change the song, or simply forget it in part or in whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:18:10-07:00","id":1387181,"title":"","content":"Hm, seeing how the Cult of the Violet Fang was described, I can see something along those lines being something that happens","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:02:18-07:00","id":1387214,"title":"","content":"Could be a Thaumaturgical ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T09:20:44-07:00","id":1387285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1387214#post1387214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be a Thaumaturgical ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you think it might need to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:13:16-07:00","id":1387326,"title":"","content":"Because Thaumaturgy need to be able to do <i>something </i> and this feels a little beyond basic applications of occult.<br /> <br /> You could have designated &quot;wayfinders&quot; whose job it is to establish the paths via thaumaturgy, and then everyone else can use them afterwards. It's the same idea but just adds a bit more nuance to the mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:05:35-07:00","id":1387336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1387326#post1387326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Thaumaturgy need to be able to do <i>something </i> and this feels a little beyond basic applications of occult.<br /> <br /> You could have designated &amp;quot;wayfinders&amp;quot; whose job it is to establish the paths via thaumaturgy, and then everyone else can use them afterwards. It's the same idea but just adds a bit more nuance to the mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn\u2019t making it thaumaturgy prevent it from being a usual practice for mortal societies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:10:08-07:00","id":1387341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1387336#post1387336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t making it thaumaturgy prevent it from being a usual practice for mortal societies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy occurs more commonly than once in ten thousand individuals, if memory serves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:19:07-07:00","id":1387343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1387341#post1387341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy occurs more commonly than once in ten thousand individuals, if memory serves.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you might find one tribe or nation with one person capable of composing a Songline, and that\u2019s assuming that anyone can employ a Songline composed by a Thaumaturge.<br /> <br /> Even then, people would need to rely on gods and Exalts to compose Songlines for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:22:50-07:00","id":1387344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386462-pretend-i-know-nothing-about-the-wyld-and-try-to-explain-it-to-me?p=1387343#post1387343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you might find one tribe or nation with one person capable of composing a Songline, and that\u2019s assuming that anyone can employ a Songline composed by a Thaumaturge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or consider the possibility that two or more tribes might share a thaumaturge between them in the interest of mutual survival.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I wouldn't really call the types of people that roam the Wyld navigating via Songlines &quot;nations.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:45:59-07:00","id":1389956,"title":"","content":"So back to the Wyld- y'all are making this too difficulty. <br /> <br /> We live in Creation. Its real. It has rules like &quot;fire is hot, water is wet&quot;. <br /> <br /> Way, way beyond the edge of the world is a land of Raw Chaos. Fire is cold, water is down, green is tomorrow, reality doesn't exist. <br /> <br /> If Creation is dirt and Chaos is Water then the Wyld is Mud. Its a mix of the two. There are some things that live there called the Fae (aka Fair Folk, aka Raksha). They are like sentient nightmares or daydreams. They are super evil and they eat dreams and emotions and intangible stuff. <br /> <br /> Don't go into the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:20:33-07:00","id":1390075,"title":"","content":"If you will forgive a late attempt to add another take. I admit it is biased according to the framing prompt:<br /> <br /> You have seen the great performances of the stage, where the dancers leap and prance to the tune of the zither. From the distant market, you hear the merry music of the peasant flute and your own feet struggle against propriety in their desire to dance. On the sea-skimming warship the rowers strain to the time of the beating drum. Even your own heart is as a metronome, keeping time to the rhythm of your life, slowing in the dull hours and racing at a lover's glance.<br /> <br /> Have you given thought to why it is that every god under Heaven has a place and purpose right to them? Why monk and shikari go to such lengths to remind all of the correct actions when they stray? Heaven is likewise a musician, playing a melody of five tones on five strings with the bow of ever-flowing time. What might those strings be? Surely you have guessed. Day and night, tick and tock, the metronome of the sky to keep the constant time. And every tone, every Pole, having its place in the score of Destiny.<br /> <br /> This is the backdrop, the stage on which we play out the music and drama of our own lives. To those who learn to hear this music, and play in harmony with it, the world holds no secrets and their will is as one with the very forces of nature. So it is with you, young Prince of the Earth. To those who strain and struggle and cry out off-key, the world is a storm that drowns out their hearts and minds with the violence of its sound.<br /> <br /> Even as the barbarians will sit on the curving hillside, and civilized folk recline in the concert hall whose seats curve this way and that to ensure they hear the proper blending of sounds, so is Creation as a bowl in which the Music of Heaven, the Chant of the Dragons, is able to be experienced as it should and strengthen itself as its echoes reinforce that which birthed them.<br /> <br /> Yet beyond the circle of the world... that is where the music grows discordant. The tone of distant Poles grows father or fainter. The music comes unraveled. Even as you might hear the strains of a distant performance and imagine you hear a different piece or even mere noise, so it is in the Wyld. Things are not in their proper relation to each other. Each element that reaches the Wyld must stand alone, divorced of context.<br /> <br /> Near to the world this discord is subtle, slight exaggerations or diminishing of this or that element of the proper order. As you go farther all descends into incohete chaos. A flower is swollen to a mountain and the aphids upon it rise up as a civilization of chitinous warriors. The heartbreak of a spurned lover spreads out until it shatters them. From such distortions arise the stories of treasures and secrets that fill cheap folios and training yard gossip.<br /> <br /> It is true you may seek out or stumble across items such as might require great sorcery or supernatural artifice to bring forth. And some may find profitable use from such things. But there is an absence, a hollowness, a wrongness at the core of such things; a flaw which will eventually destroy them. Do not forget that even the seeming humbleness of people or objects serve to strengthen all things according to the mercy and plan of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Perhaps also you have heard of people and things being changed when they venture beyond the world. This too is true, and it is a thing of brokenness more than strength. Our souls wear a carnal robe, spun from the five elements, the five tones. These too can unravel. Most often this is a most awful death, such as few tortures can equal. Some, lucky or cursed few, gain some small benefit though it can never equal what they have lost. A few will believe they are bettered by this twisting, and perhaps for some small purpose they are, yet it is damaging to the in this life and the next far beyond short-sighted gain. Those who walk the Wyld must have a sure self and a steady soul to hold themselves together against the chaos and discord that surrounds them.<br /> <br /> And as to the anathema? To the monsters that stalk the Wyld only to come as monsters to the lands of upright peoples to do mischief and murder? Yes they have such unwholesome power from the Wyld and such brokenness, most often in their warped minds. Were they limited to their own strength alone they would long ago have been destroyed by their own madness. Only the power they stole in ancient times, the steadiness of the moon who helps to keep the steadiness of time, which can endure the abuse they inflict upon themselves. It is righteous to liberate that power from their unworthy flesh. All their blasphemous works are undone and the demon must begin again without any of the seeming gain of its ill-done acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-19-2020, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}